    excerpt: 'At 6:15 AM, the world is still asleep, but inside the bedroom, hands were tracing paths across skin like explorers charting familiar rivers in the dark.',
    body: [
      'At 6:15 AM, before the city alarms began their relentless chorus, dawn filtered through the sheer linen curtains, casting ribbons of dusty rose and gold across the tangled duvet.',
      'Talia awoke to the steady rise and fall of Julian’s chest beneath her cheek. His arm was draped protectively over her waist, his fingers resting gently on the curve of her hip. She didn’t move away. Instead, she traced the small constellation of freckles across his collarbone with the tip of her forefinger.',
      'His breathing shifted. Julian stirred, his eyes opening with that slow, drowsy recognition that only comes from years of waking up together. Without saying a word, he pulled her closer until there was no daylight left between their bodies.',
      '“Good morning,” he rasped, his morning voice deep and vibrating against her throat.',
      '“You were dreaming,” she whispered, leaning in until her lips brushed the soft skin beneath his ear.',
      '“Only about you,” he answered, rolling her gently beneath him. His touch was slow, tender, and familiar, yet charged with the kind of electric desire that refused to fade with time. His lips moved from her temple to the sensitive curve of her neck, coaxing soft sighs from her parted lips.',
      'In those quiet morning minutes, love was not a grand gesture or a poetic verse. It was the rhythm of their hips, the warmth of palms pressed together with fingers interlocked, and the absolute certainty that in this bed, with this person, they were completely safe and fiercely desired.'
    ],
    reflection: 'What rituals of quiet tenderness do you maintain with those you love most? When was the last time you lingered in the morning?'
